    ($vp$APPRENTICE$vp$, 3, 1, $vp$What This Module Covers$vp$, $vp$overview$vp$, $vp$Wiring methods are the *how* of getting power from the panel to the load. The NEC doesn't tell you what brand of cable to buy — it tells you what types are allowed where, how they have to be supported, how many conductors fit in a given raceway, and how to terminate them safely.

Chapter 3 of the code is the home for almost all of this. It's also one of the biggest chapters, with dozens of articles for different cable types (NM, AC, MC, etc.) and dozens more for raceway types (EMT, RMC, IMC, PVC, FMC, LFNC, and the rest of the alphabet soup). You don't need to memorize every article number, but you need to know how to find the article for the method you're installing.

